freebsd-kvm-runner: pass /dev/kvm into the poseidon docker runner

Symptom
-------
build:freebsd works end to end (v1.8.45) but only under KVM.  On the
poseidon docker runner the job falls back to TCG because /dev/kvm is not
visible in the job container, and under TCG the FreeBSD 14.4 first boot
runs firstboot freebsd-update for ~1 h before sshd comes up (nuageinit
applies write_files too late to pre-disable it), so the job times out.
The job is allow_failure, so pipelines stay green meanwhile.

What is needed (host-side, on poseidon — needs root/runner admin)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
1. Expose /dev/kvm to the bocl-linux-docker runner (id 53805892):
   in /home/runners/.gitlab-runner/config.toml, under that runner's
   [runners.docker] section, add:

       devices = ["/dev/kvm"]

2. Make /dev/kvm usable from the ROOTLESS docker userns: the device node
   maps to nobody:nogroup inside the container, so open() fails even
   when passed through.  Simplest durable fix is a udev rule:

       # /etc/udev/rules.d/65-kvm-rootless.rules
       KERNEL=="kvm", MODE="0666"

   then `udevadm control --reload && udevadm trigger /dev/kvm`
   (a one-off `chmod 666 /dev/kvm` works until reboot).

3. Restart the runner (or `gitlab-runner restart` for the user service).

Verification
------------
Re-run build:freebsd: the log should say
    == booting FreeBSD VM (KVM) ==
and the whole job should finish in ~15-20 min.  Once it does, drop
allow_failure from the freebsd job in .gitlab-ci.yml.

Context
-------
ci/freebsd-build.sh auto-detects: KVM when /dev/kvm is writable, TCG
otherwise.  Everything else (image fetch, nuageinit seed, build, 42
test suites, linkage proof, prelude byte-compilation) was validated on
FreeBSD 14.4 under KVM on 2026-07-14.
